# Every setting the server, the worker and the web app read. Names only: copy this to .env and fill in
# what you need. The optional ones stay commented out, since a blank value replaces their default.
# With none of them set, `pnpm dev` still runs the example end to end; real scans need MODEL_API_KEY.

# ---- Meta models ----
# Meta Model API key from https://dev.meta.ai/api-keys/
MODEL_API_KEY=
# Optional: a relay in front of the Meta API (services/meta-relay). RELAY_TOKEN replaces the key there.
# META_API_BASE=
# RELAY_TOKEN=

# ---- The 3D service (services/scan3d) ----
# Locally `pnpm dev` points at the Mac runner on port 8790; in production, the Modal web endpoint
# `modal deploy` prints, and the token stored in the Modal secret `scan3d-token`. Without these the
# scan runs without 3D.
SCAN3D_URL=
SCAN3D_TOKEN=
# The as-built 3D's painting (POST /texture): a CPU endpoint (Modal's paint_web). Unset: SCAN3D_URL paints.
# SCAN3D_TEXTURE_URL=
# Areas measured side by side: 1 on the Mac, 3 on Modal (app.py max_containers).
# SCAN3D_PARALLEL=
# Frames sent per area and for the rough whole-walk pass (server/scan3d.ts, server/basement.ts).
# SCAN3D_MAX_FRAMES=
# SCAN3D_WHOLE_FRAMES=
# Dollars counted against the daily cap for each area of 3D. Defaults to 0.03 on Modal, 0 on the Mac.
# SCAN3D_USD_PER_AREA=

# ---- Limits for a public site (server/limits.ts, server/live.ts) ----
# Real scans per IP per hour (default 6), real scans per day for everyone (default 5), and what every
# paid call may cost in a day, Eastern time (default 25). The example never counts.
# SCANS_PER_IP_PER_HOUR=
# SCANS_PER_DAY=
# DAILY_COST_CAP_USD=
# Live finds while filming: SAM calls per IP per minute, per take and per day.
# LIVE_PER_IP_PER_MINUTE=
# LIVE_PER_SESSION=
# LIVE_DAILY_MAX=
# Frames the live 3D map keeps while filming (server/live3d.ts).
# LIVE3D_FRAMES=

# ---- Database and storage ----
# Postgres in production. Without it, an embedded PGlite in .data/pglite (or PGLITE_DIR).
# DATABASE_URL=
# PGLITE_DIR=
# STORAGE=r2 uses Cloudflare R2; otherwise files go to LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR (default media/private).
# STORAGE=
# LOCAL_STORAGE_DIR=
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# R2_BUCKET=

# ---- Accounts (optional, Clerk) ----
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ---- Running it ----
# API_PORT wins in dev (the preview launcher sets PORT for the web server). WORKER_INLINE=1 runs the
# job worker inside the API process on Postgres (PGlite always does).
# PORT=
# API_PORT=
# WORKER_INLINE=
# NODE_ENV=
# `pnpm dev:phone` sets this to serve the dev site over HTTPS on the Wi-Fi (scripts/dev-phone.sh).
# PHONE_CERT=
# Scripts only: where screenshot and journey scripts point, and a Chrome to drive.
# BASE_URL=
# CHROME_PATH=
